A||N||11||MikeSchaefer||P265/55R15 Rear Tires?||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||09-29-2001||11:07 PM||||Hi, Wolfhound posted that he had tried Delta Road Max P265/55R15's and they fit with about 1/8" clearance from the strut's.  Do any other brands work at this size?  What's the largest size anyone else has tried?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike Schaefer<BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cheer_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||09-30-2001||09:35 AM||||Mike here are a few shots of the clearance as well as a rear view of the car. as I said in the other post these were ordered as 245,s but were shipped wrong. The installer asked me to come look as there might be a clearance problem, that was when we discovered the error in size. the Spring reciever travels with the wheel and there have been no contact problems. Another brand may give more or less clearence. Less obviously wouldn't work.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ctire.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiresv.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rtire.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||09-30-2001||02:16 PM||||Wolfhound:<BR>Great Pics!  Those are very helpful.  As long as there is that clearance there, there's no real way for the tire to move into harms way right?  Your car looks very good with that setup btw.<P>If anyone else has experience with this please drop me a line, otherwise I'm off to the tire store in a few days.  I'll post some pic here.<BR>Thanks again,<BR>Mike Schaefer<p>[This message has been edited by MikeSchaefer (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||6
