Z||000007||Capt Fiero||09-30-2001||08:41 PM||||I rode in a car that has 245/50/16 and really did not like the washy feeling that the back end had.  If I were to go with that wide of a tire, I would really want it to be a 245/40 or a 265/35 or 30 seris tire.  Just so I do not have huge honken sidwalls. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wolfhound||10-01-2001||06:44 AM||||This car has no washy feeling, and I actually expected it to. If the tires flexed they would make contact with as little clearance as they have. It handled very well at RFTH6. They are little if any taller than the stock tire. The front are smaller.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||10-01-2001||01:01 PM||||MMmm!! Cool. That means that I can put those 265/30/19 with the Konig Veredict that Disc. tire has  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroRacer||10-01-2001||03:53 PM||||What size rims do you mount those on.  I'm starting to thing of a set of 265/35ZR18's to go on a set of 7.5 rims.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Alex4mula||10-01-2001||04:20 PM||||For a 265 low profile tire I guess you will need at least an 8.5-9 inch rim. Maybe an 8" but it may look funny.||||reg||1
